sentences.l:
Says Minaya: “now I-am satisfied,
for to Castiella will-go good tidings,
that my Çid Roy Díaz battle pitched has [won].”

sentences.t:
Traen oro e plata que non saben recabdo;
refechos son todos essos cristianos
con aquesta ganançia [que y avién fallado].

sentences.l:
They-bring gold and silver that not they-know reckoning;
remade are all those Christians
with this gain [which there they-had found].

sentences.t:
Grant a el gozo mio Çid con todos sos vassallos.
Dio a partir estos dineros e estos averes largos;
en la su quinta al Çid caen cient cavallos.

sentences.l:
Great has the joy my Çid with all his vassals.
He-gave to divide these monies and these riches abundant;
in the his fifth to-the Çid fall a-hundred horses.

sentences.t:
—“Evades aquí oro e plata [fina],
una uesa lleña, que nada nol mingua;
en Santa María de Burgos quitedes mill missas;

sentences.l:
—“Behold here gold and silver [fine],
a boot full, that nothing not-to-it lacks;
in Santa María of Burgos you-pay-for a-thousand masses;

sentences.t:
lo que romaneçiere daldo a mi mugier e a mis fijas,
que rueguen por mí las noches e los días;
si les yo visquier[o], serán dueñas ricas.”

sentences.l:
what that may-remain give-it to my wife and to my daughters,
that they-pray for me the nights and the days;
if for-them I should-live, they-will-be ladies rich.”

By lances and by swords we-have to survive,
if not, in this land narrow not we-could live,
and as I think, to go ourselves we-shall-have from here.”
